+# Static IPFS Deployment
+
+These commands build and verify the static site. They do not upload anything until the explicit `ipfs add` step.
+
+## 1. Prepare the fork deployment
+
+The static app needs the generated local fork contract address. Start the Base fork and deploy first:
+
+```bash
+yarn fork
+```
+
+In another terminal:
+
+```bash
+yarn deploy
+```
+
+Confirm `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` contains `USDCTipJar` under chain ID `31337`.
+
+## 2. Build the static export
+
+Set the public origin you will use for the published site. Prefer a stable gateway, ENS, IPNS, or custom domain because this value is embedded in metadata.
+
+```bash
+export NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL=https://tips.example.com
+
+cd packages/nextjs
+rm -rf .next out
+NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_BUILD=true \
+NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL=$NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL \
+yarn build
+```
+
+Verify the export shape:
+
+```bash
+test -f out/index.html
+test -f out/debug/index.html
+test -f out/blockexplorer/index.html
+grep -R "$NEXT_PUBLIC_PRODUCTION_URL" out/index.html
+```
+
+## 3. Upload to IPFS
+
+With a local Kubo node:
+
+```bash
+ipfs daemon
+```
+
+In another terminal from `packages/nextjs`:
+
+```bash
+CID=$(ipfs add -Qr out)
+echo "CID=$CID"
+```
+
+With a remote pinning service, upload the contents of `packages/nextjs/out` as a directory and record the returned CID.
+
+## 4. Post-deploy verification
+
+Replace `<cid>` and `<gateway>` with the CID and gateway you use.
+
+```bash
+export CID=<cid>
+export GATEWAY=https://ipfs.io
+
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/"
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/debug/"
+curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" -L "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/blockexplorer/"
+curl -sL "$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/" | grep "Base USDC Tip Jar"
+```
+
+Expected status code for each route is `200`.
+
+For an interactive smoke test through the gateway, keep the local Base fork running at `http://127.0.0.1:8545`, keep the browser wallet on chain ID `31337`, open `$GATEWAY/ipfs/$CID/`, approve USDC, and send a small tip. Then verify the USDC balances against the local fork:
+
+```bash
+export RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
+export USDC=0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913
+export TIPPER_A=0xf39fd6e51aad88f6f4ce6ab8827279cfffb92266
+export RECIPIENT=0xa0Ee7A142d267C1f36714E4a8F75612F20a79720
+
+cast call $USDC "balanceOf(address)(uint256)" $TIPPER_A --rpc-url $RPC_URL
+cast call $USDC "balanceOf(address)(uint256)" $RECIPIENT --rpc-url $RPC_URL
+```
